Component Props type Notes <code>KubeObjectListLayout</code> <code>KubeObjectListLayoutProps&lt;K,A,D&gt;</code> The full resource list page: search, filters, namespace select, columns, per-row menu. Needs <code>store</code>. <code>KubeObjectDetails</code> — Host for the details drawer (usually you register a <code>Details</code> component instead). <code>KubeObjectMenu</code> <code>KubeObjectMenuProps&lt;T&gt;</code> Context/action menu for an object. <code>KubeObjectMeta</code> <code>KubeObjectMetaProps</code> Standard metadata rows (name/ns/labels/age). <code>KubeObjectAge</code> <code>KubeObjectAgeProps</code> Age cell. <code>KubeObjectConditionsList</code> / <code>KubeObjectConditionsDrawer</code> … Render <code>status.conditions</code>. <code>LinkTo*</code> per-file Cross-links: <code>LinkToNamespace</code>, <code>LinkToPod</code>, <code>LinkToNode</code>, <code>LinkToSecret</code>, <code>LinkToConfigMap</code>, <code>LinkToJob</code>, <code>LinkToReplicaSet</code>, <code>LinkToRole</code>, <code>LinkToClusterRole</code>, <code>LinkToServiceAccount</code>, <code>LinkToStorageClass</code>, <code>LinkToPriorityClass</code>, <code>LinkToRuntimeClass</code>, <code>LinkToObject</code>, … <code>ItemListLayout</code> <code>ItemListLayoutProps&lt;Item,…&gt;</code> Generic (non-kube) list layout. <p><code>KubeObjectDetailsProps&lt;T&gt;</code> (<code>{ className?; object: T }</code>) is the props type your registered detail components receive.</p> <p>Minimal list page:</p> <pre><code>&lt;KubeObjectListLayout&lt;Example, ExampleApi&gt;
  tableId="examplesTable"
  store={Example.getStore&lt;Example&gt;()}
  sortingCallbacks={{ name: (o) =&gt; o.getName(), age: (o) =&gt; o.getCreationTimestamp() }}
  searchFilters={[(o) =&gt; o.getSearchFields()]}
  renderHeaderTitle={Example.crd.title}
  renderTableHeader={[{ title: "Name", sortBy: "name" }, /* … */]}
  renderTableContents={(o) =&gt; [o.getName(), &lt;KubeObjectAge object={o} key="age" /&gt;]}
/&gt;
</code></pre>

Component / object Notes <code>Dialog</code> Modal dialog (<code>DialogProps</code>). <code>LogsDialog</code> Log viewer dialog. <code>ConfirmDialog</code> Confirm modal. Statics: <code>ConfirmDialog.open(params)</code> and <code>ConfirmDialog.confirm(params): Promise&lt;boolean&gt;</code>. Params: <code>ConfirmDialogParams</code> (<code>message</code>, <code>labelOk</code>, <code>labelCancel</code>, <code>icon</code>, …). <code>Notifications</code> Object with <code>.ok / .error / .checkedError / .info / .shortInfo</code>. <code>notificationsStore</code> The notifications store instance. <pre><code>const { Notifications } = Renderer.Component;
Notifications.error("Something failed");
if (await Renderer.Component.ConfirmDialog.confirm({ message: "Delete?" })) { /* … */ }
</code></pre>

Export Purpose <code>catalogEntities</code> Entity registry: <code>.activeEntity</code>, <code>.entities</code> (Map), <code>.getById(id)</code>, <code>.getItemsForApiKind&lt;T&gt;(apiVersion, kind)</code>, <code>.getItemsForCategory&lt;T&gt;(category)</code>, <code>.addOnBeforeRun(hook): Disposer</code>. <code>catalogCategories</code> The category registry (same object as <code>Main.Catalog.catalogCategories</code>); register your <code>CatalogCategory</code> subclass here. <code>activeCluster</code> The active <code>KubernetesCluster</code> entity. <code>getAllClusters()</code> <code>() =&gt; ClusterInfo[]</code>. <code>getClusterById(id)</code> <code>(ClusterId) =&gt; ClusterInfo \| undefined</code>. <code>getActiveCluster()</code> <code>() =&gt; ClusterInfo \| undefined</code>. <p><code>ClusterInfo</code> (<code>Common.Clusters</code>):</p> <pre><code>interface ClusterInfo {
  id: ClusterId;
  name: string;
  kubeConfigPath: string;
  contextName: string;
  status: ClusterConnectionStatus;   // CONNECTING | CONNECTED | DISCONNECTED | DISCONNECTING
  labels: Record&lt;string, string&gt;;
  isActive: boolean;
  metadata?: ClusterMetadata;
}

interface ClusterMetadata {          // extended, may be absent
  distribution?: string;             // "eks" | "gke" | "aks" | "minikube" | …
  kubernetesVersion?: string;        // "1.28.0"
  nodeCount?: number;
  lastConnected?: Date;
  connectionError?: string;
}
</code></pre>
